# All in the loop is proven: the object is never made, the method is copied. What was left in each turn is the check of the dead zone of `Point`, whose value nobody reads.
# A variable of a body that runs once never goes back into its dead zone: it is asked once, in front of the loop. Where it is empty the other copy runs, which stands first in the text and is built for its size:
# it checks in its turn, and throws where the program does. This program never sees that: Bun moves the declaration of such a class in front of the statements of its module, with or without --aot.
# The two tests beside this one enter their loops in a dead zone.
# OPTIONS: check=Validate
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: = GetModuleVariable
# CHECK-NEXT: = TypeTest {{*}}testedType=absent
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch
# CHECK: frequency=Rare isLoopHead=true
# CHECK: = CheckInitialized {{*}}name="Point"
# CHECK: isInLoop=true isLoopHead=true
# CHECK-NOT: = CheckInitialized
# CHECK-NOT: = GetModuleVariable
# CHECK: Return
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell
# ANSWERS: 0 9
# ANSWERS-NEXT: 0 9
